      "claim": "The narrowest bony dimension of the adult female pelvis (the obstetric conjugate) is ≈110 mm, and even with maximal physiological soft‑tissue stretching the functional transverse diameter of the pelvic outlet rarely exceeds 130 mm.",
      "evidence": "Obstetrics textbooks and clinical studies of pelvic dimensions (e.g., Cunningham et al., 2014; measurements of maximal pelvic outlet expansion during labor).",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The skull’s smallest dimension (140 mm) is larger than the largest achievable transverse diameter of the birth canal (≈130 mm) by at least 10 mm.",
